  "question_stem": "Maryam has 7 sweets in a tin; 6 are toffees and 1 is a chocolate. She chooses one sweet at random and takes it out. Her friend adds 3 chocolates to the tin. Then Maryam takes another sweet at random out of the tin.",
  "context_texts": [
    "The tree has first-draw probabilities T $6/7$, C $1/7$; after T the second probabilities are T $5/9$, C $4/9$, and after C they are T $6/9$, C $3/9$.",
    "The number of toffees $X$ has distribution $P(X=0)=3/63$, $P(X=1)=30/63$, $P(X=2)=30/63$.",
    "The relevant paths are C then T with probability $(1/7)(6/9)$ and T then T with probability $(6/7)(5/9)$."
  ],
